"<p>Nitrobase monitors versioned apps (marketplace templates, standalone databases, and Git branches) for newer releases and provides one-click or automated backup-first updates with rollback protection.</p>\n<h2>Update Checks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Scheduled via <code>APP_UPDATE_CHECK_CRON</code> (default <code>41 */6 * * *</code>, every 6 hours) when <code>APP_UPDATE_CHECK_ENABLED=true</code>.</li>\n<li>Git branch tip checks can be toggled independently with <code>APP_UPDATE_CHECK_GIT=true</code>.</li>\n<li>Available updates appear with an <strong>Update available</strong> badge on the dashboard, sidebar, and app list, and trigger the <code>app.update_available</code> notification event.</li>\n<li>Bulk updates let you update up to <code>50</code> apps (<code>APP_UPDATE_BATCH_MAX</code>) in a single batch.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Safe Update Pipeline</h2>\n<p>When an update runs:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Pre-update backup:</strong> Enabled by default (mandatory for automatic updates). Creates a full backup before modifying the app.</li>\n<li><strong>Deploy new version:</strong> Resolves the new release/commit, renders updated config/overlays, pulls or builds images, and restarts services.</li>\n<li><strong>Readiness &#x26; stability verification:</strong> Waits for HTTP health probes and ensures every container stays ready with no restarts over <code>APP_READY_STABLE_MS</code> (default <code>20s</code>, <code>3</code> consecutive samples) and does not hit <code>APP_DEPLOY_RESTART_LIMIT</code> (default <code>6</code> restarts).</li>\n<li><strong>Automatic rollback on failure:</strong> Behavior is determined by the template or database engine's <code>[updates].rollback</code> policy:\n<ul>\n<li><code>redeploy</code> (default): Redeploys the previous pinned version/commit (data untouched).</li>\n<li><code>restore</code>: Restores the pre-update backup (used when a new version migrates data files irreversibly, such as MariaDB or Valkey forward upgrades). If no backup was taken, falls back to <code>manual</code> so old binaries are never started against migrated data.</li>\n<li><code>manual</code>: Leaves the app for operator intervention and emits <code>app.update_failed</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Automatic Updates &#x26; Maintenance Windows</h2>\n<p>Under an app's <strong>Update policy</strong> (<code>app.update_policy.manage</code> permission), you can opt in to automatically apply <strong>patch</strong> or <strong>minor</strong> semver releases (non-semver versions are never auto-applied):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Automatic updates always take a backup first.</li>\n<li>New automatic updates only start inside the configured maintenance window: <code>APP_AUTO_UPDATE_CRON</code> (default <code>0 3 * * *</code>, daily at 03:00) for <code>APP_AUTO_UPDATE_WINDOW_MINUTES</code> (default <code>120</code> minutes).</li>\n</ul>"